# L1 / B008 — dependency-injection, development-workflow, docker, dotnet-testing, ef-core, git-workflow, health-check.

C R200 OL GOV-002 | MUST | For a new application or substantial feature read SPECIFICATION.md (and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md) before planning or implementing. | new applications and substantial features | none stated
C R201 OL GOV-018 | MUST | Before implementing a questionable request name the concrete concerns (duplication, poor cohesion, trigger or loading problems, context cost, architecture conflict, unnecessary complexity) and propose an alternative; this never authorizes silently rewriting or ignoring the user's requirement. | questionable requests | none stated
C R202 OL RUN-012 | MUST | A performance-motivated change identifies the actual bottleneck, preserves observable behavior, uses the simplest optimization that addresses it, adds or keeps tests for affected behavior, and benchmarks or profiles non-obvious or complex optimizations. | performance changes | none stated
C R203 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run code-review (or the code-reviewer agent) before final verification. | substantial work | none stated
C R204 OL WF-003 | MUST | Before declaring implementation complete (and before preparing a PR) run verify at the scope and risk of the change; work is not complete until its verify step has run. | implementation completion | none stated
C R205 OL GOV-015 | MUST NOT | Do not commit, push, merge, rebase, reset, force-push, delete or rename branches, or perform other repository-changing Git operations unless explicitly requested. | Git operations | Explicit request.
C R206 OL GOV-016 | MUST | Parallel implementation work uses separate branches or worktrees (one branch is never checked out in several normal worktrees); keep unrelated changes out of the current branch. | parallel work | none stated
C R207 OL GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Never discard, overwrite, reset, clean, stash away or otherwise destroy user work to make a Git operation easier; never remove a worktree holding uncommitted user work; never stash, reset or discard automatically to let a merge or rebase proceed. | Git operations | none stated
C R208 OL GOV-020 | MUST | Before any repository-changing operation inspect the relevant state (status, diffs, current branch, upstream, what high-risk operations would lose or rewrite) and use the minimum operation that achieves the request; never silently clean unrelated working-tree changes. | Git operations | none stated
C R209 OL WF-022 | MUST | Before committing inspect the staged diff and include only the requested logical change; never stage unrelated modified files; one logical change per commit with implementation and its tests together; no unrelated fixes bundled; avoid pushing unrelated local commits. | commits and pushes | none stated
C U2 LU GOV-015 | MUST NOT (conditional) | High-risk Git operations (reset --hard, clean, push --force, push --force-with-lease, branch deletion, rebasing shared history) run only when explicitly requested or required by an approved workflow, and only after inspecting what will be lost or rewritten. | Git operations | 'required by an approved workflow' | GOV-015 allows repository-changing Git operations only on explicit request; the alternative trigger 'required by an approved workflow' names no such workflow and could authorize high-risk operations without an explicit request, or could merely refer to an explicitly approved procedure. The relation to GOV-015 cannot be settled from the text. | Under the broad reading an agent could force-push or delete a branch because a workflow 'requires' it, without the user's explicit request.
C X26 EX WF-009 | MUST | The development-workflow output summarizes what changed, Delegated decisions taken, open Decision Requests (Reserved) and the verify report. | implementation work | none stated | WF-009 covers verification state and GOV-017 reporting of unresolved Decision Requests in headless runs; listing Delegated decisions in every implementation summary is an additional reporting duty. | A final summary that omits the Delegated decisions taken does not follow the workflow.
C X27 EX GOV-015,GOV-019 | MUST NOT | Treat main, master and other protected or shared branches as non-rewritable. | Git history rewriting | none stated | GOV-015 permits repository-changing operations, including force-push and rebase, when explicitly requested; this rule forbids rewriting these branches without an approval path. | Even when the user explicitly asks to force-push a rewritten main, the instruction tells the agent not to rewrite it.
C X28 EX WF-009 | MUST | A pull request stays focused and its description states what changed, why, how it was verified, and compatibility or migration notes. | pull request preparation | none stated | No oracle policy prescribes PR description contents; WF-009 only requires truthful verification reporting. | A PR prepared without verification or migration notes does not follow the workflow.

